I personally don't think this is an improvement in this context:
```c++
if (fs_case_sensitive) {
	if (fs->files[i]->file == file) {
		cpos = i;
		break;
	}
} else {
	if (fs->files[i]->file.to_lower() == file.to_lower()) {
		cpos = i;
		break;
	}
}
```
The two inner conditions fulfill the same purpose, which IMHO is much easier to read if they are on the same indentation level.

For reference an analogous condition in this style already exists [here](https://github.com/HolonProduction/godot/blob/a1edb9ca3862dc36a084d282ea6de32befb52fdd/editor/editor_file_system.cpp#L1893-L1903).

But yeah, not my decision to make I guess :shrug:

